:[{"text":"மாசு","lemma":"மாசு","gloss":"dirt"},{"text":"உண்","lemma":"உண்","gloss":"have/eat"}],"gloss":"dirty"},{"surface":"உடுக்கை","parts":[{"text":"உடுக்கை","lemma":"உடுக்கை","gloss":"clothing"}],"gloss":"clothing"},{"surface":"மடிவாய்","parts":[{"text":"மடி","lemma":"மடி","gloss":"fold/whistle"},{"text":"வாய்","lemma":"வாய்","gloss":"mouth"}],"gloss":"whistling mouth"},{"surface":"இடையன்","parts":[{"text":"இடை","lemma":"இடை","gloss":"middle/herdsman"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"அன்","gloss":"masculine singular suffix"}],"gloss":"shepherd"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சிறுதலை","parts":[{"text":"சிறு","lemma":"சிறு","gloss":"small"},{"text":"தலை","lemma":"தலை","gloss":"head"}],"gloss":"small-headed"},{"surface":"ஆயமொடு","parts":[{"text":"ஆயம்","lemma":"ஆயம்","gloss":"flock/herd"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"ஒடு","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with his flock"},{"surface":"குறுகல்","parts":[{"text":"குறுகு","lemma":"குறுகு","gloss":"approach"},{"text":"அல்","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"approaching"},{"surface":"செல்லாப்","parts":[{"text":"செல்","lemma":"செல்","gloss":"go"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ஆ","gloss":"negative participle suffix"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"ப்","gloss":"sandhi consonant"}],"gloss":"unable to go"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புலிதுஞ்சு","parts":[{"text":"புலி","lemma":"புலி","gloss":"tiger"},{"text":"துஞ்சு","lemma":"துஞ்சு","gloss":"sleep"}],"gloss":"where a tiger sleeps"},{"surface":"வியன்புலத்து","parts":[{"text":"வியன்","lemma":"வியன்","gloss":"vast"},{"text":"புலத்து","lemma":"புலம்","gloss":"land-oblique"}],"gloss":"vast forest/land"},{"surface":"அற்றே","parts":[{"text":"அற்று","lemma":"அற்று","gloss":"like that"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"is like that"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வலிதுஞ்சு","parts":[{"text":"வலி","lemma":"வலி","gloss":"strength"},{"text":"துஞ்சு","lemma":"துஞ்சு","gloss":"abide"}],"gloss":"where strength abides"},{"surface":"தடக்கை","parts":[{"text":"தட","lemma":"தட","gloss":"broad/large"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"க்","gloss":"sandhi consonant"},{"text":"கை","lemma":"கை","gloss":"hand/arm"}],"gloss":"broad hands"},{"surface":"அவனுடை","parts":[{"text":"அவன்","lemma":"அவன்","gloss":"he"},{"text":"உடை","lemma":"உடை","gloss":"possessive suffix"}],"gloss":"his"},{"surface":"நாடே","parts":[{"text":"நாடு","lemma":"நாடு","gloss":"country"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"country indeed"}]}],"literal":"Our king resided bustling ancient town / those who possess like without hindrance approaching / lord's daily assembly with heads held high entering / like our life to suppliants is indeed easy / to suppliants easy of access not only generosity accepting / the sky/clouds to feel ashamed without limit to those who go to him / unceasingly giving open-handed generous / swift horses Kothai opposing his strength who rose up / boastful words kings when they think at the time / green leaves strung of twigs chaplet / dirty clothing whistling mouth shepherd / small-headed with his flock approaching unable to go / where a tiger sleeps vast forest/land is like that / where strength abides broad hands his country indeed","translation":"For suppliants like us, it is easy to enter with heads held high into the daily assembly of our great lord, approaching without any hindrance, just like those who own the bustling ancient town where our king resides. Kothai, who has swift horses and open-handed generosity, who gives endlessly and without limit to those who come to him, so much so that the rain-clouds feel ashamed, is easy of access to suppliants. But when the boastful kings who rise up opposing his strength think of him, his country, ruled by his broad hands where strength abides, is like a vast forest where a tiger sleeps, which a dirty-clothed shepherd wearing a chaplet of green leaves and twigs, with a whistling mouth, cannot approach with his flock of small-headed sheep.","modern":"எங்கள் அரசன் வாழ்கின்ற ஆரவாரமிக்க பழமையான ஊரைத் தமக்குச் சொந்தமாகக் கொண்டவர்களைப் போல, எவ்விதத் தடையுமின்றி நெருங்கி, அவனது சிறந்த நாளவைக்குள் தலைநிமிர்ந்து நுழைவது எங்களைப் போன்ற இரவலர்களுக்கு மிகவும் எளிதானது. இரவலர்களுக்கு எளிமையாக விளங்குவதோடு மட்டுமல்லாமல், கொடையை ஏற்றுக்கொண்டு, மேகம் நாணும்படி எல்லையின்றித் தன்னிடம் வருவோருக்கு இடைவிடாது வழங்கும் கவிகை போன்ற வள்ளல் தன்மையையும், வேகமான குதிரைகளையும் உடையவன் கோதை. அவனது வலிமையை எதிர்த்துப் போரிட எழுந்த வஞ்சின மொழிகளைக் கூறும் பகை அரசர்கள் நினைத்துப் பார்க்கும் காலத்தில், வலிமை தங்கிய பெரிய கைகளைக் கொண்ட அவனுடைய நாடானது, பச்சிலை மற்றும் தழைகளால் தொடுக்கப்பட்ட மாலையையும் அழுக்கடைந்த ஆடையையும் உடைய, வாயைக் குவித்து விசில் ஊதும் இடையன் தன் சிறிய தலையையுடைய ஆட்டு மந்தையுடன் நெருங்க முடியாதவாறு புலி படுத்திருக்கும் பரந்த காட்டைப் போன்றதாகும்.","explanation":"The poet Madalan Madurai Kumaranar praises the Chera king Kuttuvan Kothai, highlighting his contrasting nature towards suppliants and enemies. To the poets and beggars, the king is extremely accessible; they can enter his royal court with heads held high, feeling as if they own the city. The king's generosity is so boundless that even the rain-clouds feel ashamed of their limits. However, to the hostile kings who boast of their strength, Kothai's territory is terrifyingly unapproachable. The poet uses a vivid pastoral image: his land is like a vast forest where a tiger sleeps, which a simple shepherd with his flock of sheep dares not enter. This comparison beautifully illustrates the theme of Aracavākai, celebrating both the protective benevolence and the formidable power of the ruler.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}